---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SEOHead from '../components/SEOHead.astro';
import { url } from '../utils/paths';
---
<Base title="Marketing for endurance and sports brands" description="Manual Focus is a Sheffield marketing agency for endurance brands. We get the brand in focus before launch, then keep the marketing working all season.">
  <SEOHead slot="seo" type="service" title="Marketing for endurance and sports brands" description="Manual Focus is a Sheffield marketing agency for endurance brands. We get the brand in focus before launch, then keep the marketing working all season." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Services', url: '/services/' }]} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">SERVICES</div>
      <h1>Marketing for endurance and sports brands</h1>
      <p class="lead">Manual Focus is a marketing agency in Sheffield for endurance and sports brands. We sharpen the brand first, then launch your products with campaigns and content. Your own team or PR agency runs the PR from a plan we write with you. After launch week we build the website and email marketing that keep selling all season. You can buy the work in four ways, set out below. Every engagement starts with a free 30-minute working session.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Strategic Advisor -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/01 · STRATEGIC ADVISOR</div>
        <h2>Your team ships work without anyone steering.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits companies with a marketing team but no senior leader running it.</p>
        <p>You have people doing the work but nobody senior to call the shots. Nobody reviews the output or asks the harder questions. We sit alongside the team for a handful of sessions a month. You get a CMO's strategic input without the cost or commitment of hiring one.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Weekly or fortnightly working sessions on what to do next</li>
          <li>Reviews of campaigns and creative before they ship</li>
          <li>Quarterly planning and priority-setting with the team</li>
          <li>Hiring and team-shape advice as you grow the function</li>
          <li>Advice on which AI tools are worth your team's time</li>
          <li>A direct line between sessions for the calls that won't wait</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What stays with your team</h3>
        <p>Your team keeps running itself and shipping the work. We join a handful of meetings a month rather than all of them. If you want someone embedded in your leadership team, that's the Fractional CMO.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · 1–2 days a month, on a day rate or monthly retainer</p>
        <p class="service-proof">James works this way with companies that use AI to manage people's wealth.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/contact/')}?offer=strategic-advisor`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fractional CMO -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/02 · FRACTIONAL CMO</div>
        <h2>You need a part-time CMO.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits companies that need senior marketing leadership without making a full-time hire.</p>
        <p>We join your leadership team and set the marketing thesis. Then we build the plan and lead the people you already have. The pieces that need senior hands, we ship ourselves. We use AI for the repetitive work, so a small team gets through the work of a much larger one. You get a CMO's seniority for a fraction of the cost, with the work shipping alongside the strategy.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A marketing thesis and a 90-day plan</li>
          <li>Quarterly OKRs</li>
          <li>Leading and growing the existing team (or hiring it)</li>
          <li>Shipping the key campaigns and launches</li>
          <li>A say in pricing and positioning</li>
          <li>Input into product decisions</li>
          <li>Owning reporting to the CEO and board</li>
          <li>Marketing automations that give your team time back</li>
          <li>Shorter production cycles, with AI doing the repetitive work</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What to expect</h3>
        <p>You get a senior marketer who ships the work as well as planning it. The seat is part-time by design, so we set the cadence to make the most of one or two days a week.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · 1–2 days a week, three-month minimum</p>
        <p class="service-proof">James led marketing from the inside at RGT Cycling, where he was on the founding team before Wahoo bought it. He has also led marketing for a privacy-focused crypto project worth $400M.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/contact/')}?offer=fractional-cmo`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Build & Hand Over -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/03 · BUILD &amp; HAND OVER</div>
        <h2>You know what you need built.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits companies that want a specific piece of marketing shipped fast.</p>
        <p>You might want a brand refresh or a product launch. Maybe it's a new website or an email programme. We build it end to end. Then we hand it back to your team to run, with documentation and training to keep it going.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Brand refreshes with messaging architecture and visual direction</li>
          <li>Product or feature launches, built on clear positioning and a strong narrative</li>
          <li>PR planning and overall strategy, for your in-house team or PR agency to run</li>
          <li>Fast commerce rebuilds on Shopify or BigCommerce</li>
          <li>WooCommerce and WordPress builds, full-stack or headless</li>
          <li>Headless web builds on composable stacks, made for speed and a clean handover</li>
          <li>Landing systems and conversion infrastructure, built in Astro or Webflow as the job needs</li>
          <li>Email programmes that keep selling after the launch</li>
          <li>SEO and answer-engine optimisation programmes, including content engines</li>
          <li>Marketing automations built into your existing stack</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How it ends</h3>
        <p>We fix the scope and the price up front. Once the build ships we hand it over, so your team owns it from then on.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · Fixed price for a fixed scope, with most builds taking 4–12 weeks</p>
        <p class="service-proof">You can see the method on our own site in the <a href={url('/lens/ops/site-audit-and-refresh/')}>September 2026 audit and refresh</a>, with the retest logs published.</p>
        <p class="service-proof">Planning a website or a rebrand? <a href={url('/brief/')}>Send the six-question brief</a> and James will reply with what to fix first.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/contact/')}?offer=build-and-hand-over`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- /04 Content we run for you, sold as Manual Focus AI -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail service-detail-product reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/04 · CONTENT WE RUN FOR YOU <span class="service-tag-flag">RETAINER</span></div>
        <h2>Your team can't keep up with the content.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">This suits brands whose teams have no time to build content pipelines or learn another tool every week.</p>
        <p>We plan the content and produce it for you, wireframes included. It arrives in your brand on an agreed schedule. We use AI for the heavy production work. When a better model ships we swap it in, so the output keeps improving without your team learning a new tool.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Content planning that takes a calendar through to fact-checked drafts</li>
          <li>Wireframes and creative for landing pages and ads</li>
          <li>Social packs, ready to post</li>
          <li>A weekly digest of competitor moves and search ranking shifts</li>
          <li>Output in your brand and your stack, ready to use</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What your team does</h3>
        <p>Your team has nobody to manage and no tool to learn. We tune the work to your brand and deliver it on the agreed schedule.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · Monthly retainer with a three-month minimum</p>
        <p class="service-proof">You can see it running in the <a href={url('/lens/content/news-desk/')}>news desk</a> behind our own AI briefing. Only the day's stories that clear the bar get published.</p>
        <p class="service-proof">This retainer is sold as Manual Focus AI. You may also hear us call the senior team the Foundry and its shared AI toolkit the Forge.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/contact/')}?offer=manual-focus-ai`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Specialism note -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">WHERE WE WORK</div>
      <h2 class="vertical-headline">Endurance and sports brands<br/>are where we've shipped the most.</h2>
      <p class="vertical-copy">If you're building in endurance or the wider fitness category, you get a team that has run marketing in your category at scale. James Vickers, our founder, was on the founding team at RGT Cycling, which Wahoo Fitness later bought. Outside sport we've led marketing in AI and fintech, so the playbook travels. For search, read the <a href={url('/blog/seo-playbook-premium-endurance-brands/')}>SEO playbook for premium endurance brands</a>. If you're a B2B or corporate company outside sport, read <a href={url('/business/')}>how we work with businesses</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">WHAT HAPPENS NEXT</div>
      <ol class="next-steps-list">
        <li><strong>We meet for a free 30-minute working session.</strong> You bring the problem. We bring questions and a first view on it.</li>
        <li><strong>If it's a fit, you get a written scope.</strong> It sets out the shape of the engagement and the cost. Builds get a fixed price up front.</li>
        <li><strong>We start.</strong> On a Fractional CMO engagement, we set the thesis and a 90-day plan in the first month.</li>
      </ol>
      <a href={url('/contact/')} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .service-detail {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
  }

  /* Product tier — distinct from the three engagement tiers above */
  .service-detail-product {
    position: relative;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(192, 38, 211, 0.05), rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.02)),
      var(--color-bg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .service-detail-product::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--color-cta-gradient);
  }
  .service-tag-flag {
    margin-left: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-cta-end);
    color: var(--color-cta-end);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    background: rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.06);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .service-detail-product { padding: var(--space-lg); }
  }

  .service-tag {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .service-for {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail > p {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .service-detail ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail ul li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .service-proof {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .service-proof a,
  .vertical-copy a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }

  .next-steps-list {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .next-steps-list strong { color: var(--color-text); }

  .service-shape {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .vertical-headline {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .vertical-copy {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
</style>
